<h2>3. The left distribution chooses the bill</h2>

<p>
The discrete case makes the accounting visible. Each outcome contributes
$q_i\log(q_i/p_i)$. If $q_i=0$, that outcome contributes nothing, no matter how large
$p_i$ is. If $q_i>0$ and $p_i=0$, the KL is infinite: $p$ says an event that actually
happens is impossible.
</p>

